  <!-- =================================================================
       ThingFilter tree-navigation state (ThingFilterNavigationState).
       The newer tree-based filter UI used by ReadingPolicyEditorState
       (and others wired during D.7 follow-ups) shares the Storage.*
       keys above for navigation and toggle announcements; only the
       slider-edit mode is unique. Pressing Enter on a HitPoints or
       Quality row enters edit mode where Left/Right adjusts the active
       part (Min or Max) and Up/Down swaps parts.

       SliderPart.Min / SliderPart.Max are the bare part-name nouns,
       composed into the edit-mode announcement and the per-part value
       readout. SliderEdit.Announcement: {0} = slider name (vanilla
       "Quality" or "HitPointsBasic"), {1} = part name, {2} = value.
       Spoken once on entering edit mode; the keyboard-hint sentence
       is part of the key so word order can vary per language.
       SliderEdit.PartWithValue: {0} = part name, {1} = value. Spoken
       when switching parts via Up/Down.
       ================================================================= -->
  <RimWorldAccess.Inspection.ThingFilter.SliderPart.Min>Minimum</RimWorldAccess.Inspection.ThingFilter.SliderPart.Min>
  <RimWorldAccess.Inspection.ThingFilter.SliderPart.Max>Maximum</RimWorldAccess.Inspection.ThingFilter.SliderPart.Max>
  <RimWorldAccess.Inspection.ThingFilter.SliderEdit.Announcement>{0} - {1}: {2}. Use Left/Right to adjust, Up/Down to switch Min/Max, Enter to confirm.</RimWorldAccess.Inspection.ThingFilter.SliderEdit.Announcement>
